  "contracts": [
    "Native annotations are optional version1 selection metadata with exact vertex count, counter0..99 and optional complete zero-based scientific T/C/Z; preserve unrelated attributes. Reject malformed/version/unknown fields, negative/out-of-extent positions and mismatched counts.",
    "Explicit ImageJ wire adapters use low8 counter, high24 C-fastest one-based stack position, zero unbound. Signed-position overflow and unsupported counter/extent refuse. Raw byte codec retains its separate sidecars and does not silently consume semantic attributes.",
    "Single-point measurement ignores its stored per-point position like original Analyzer, retaining the annotation. Multipoint explicit positions override captured parent axes; unbound points use parent stored/view axes.",
    "Counter populations count all parent vertices, independent of plane grouping. Expose point_counter metadata; point_counter_count and Counter/Count columns exist only with multiple used counters. Point index remains separate.",
    "Manager request includes exactly the acquired point positions, without an unused parent plane. Preserve parent/vertex order, frozen source/calibration, original pixel statistics and grouped source validation/lookup.",
    "Version6 diagnostic records add annotation policy/counters; earlier diagnostic meanings and unannotated row behavior remain unchanged. Not executable replay.",
    "Python bridges own argument values before GIL release; dataset extent conversion uses the existing reviewed shape helper. Metadata helpers dispatch no provider callbacks."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "M2b.2 must expose annotation editing controls and connect real importer/exporter mappings and vertex insert/delete/point-tool metadata preservation; no complete point-tool UI claim.",
    "Automatic XZ/YZ mapping and explicit rebind/wire projection policy remain owned by M2b.2 with T06/T10. Current explicit adapter is for XY hyperstack semantics.",
    "M2b.3 manager MultiMeasure/Z/T variants, M3 area/shape/threshold/redirect, M4 reconciliation and T04a.3 session/recorder/replay remain open.",
    "Existing native session preserves annotation attributes in a focused roundtrip; this does not establish complete analysis session/replay support.",
    "Finite scalar UInt8/UInt16/Float32 measurements; no broad RGB/IEEE, Linux/macOS UI, release/ABI compatibility or matched processing-speed superiority claim.",
    "Storage remains unverified with214 inaccessible subtrees; local captures require archive restoration."
  ],
  "waste_review": {
    "fixed": [
      "Each factory/preparation pass decodes annotations once per parent; count populations once per prepared parent, preserving grouped source reads and one lookup instead of per-point acquisitions.",
      "Reuse shared metadata/session/statistics/jobs/formatter/probe and existing shape conversion rather than new controllers/runners.",
      "Clean the new misleading-indentation warning before installed-client verification.",
      "Correct seven test setups to the actual read-only Selection binding constructor and retry only those failed IDs."
    ],
    "deferred": [
      {
        "owner": "T02 and next task validation owner",
        "work": "Binding-assumption failures recurred despite the existing preflight rule. Inspect the exact owning Python constructor/getter signatures before writing next setup assertions.",
